.TH PROFILE 4 "31 October 2026" "amix-base"
.SH NAME
profile \- the login shell's start-up commands for every user
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/profile
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B /etc/profile
is read by
.BR sh (1)
and
.BR ksh (1)
when they start as a login shell, before the user's own
.BR $HOME/.profile .
The file shipped with the base package is the system's own, from release
2.1p2a, with one addition at its end.
.PP
The system's part:
.IP \(bu 3
sets
.B PATH
(the stock directories, with
.B /usr/local/bin
first and, for users other than root,
.B $HOME/bin
before it and the current directory at its end) and
.BR TERM
(on the console, the console's terminal type), and exports
.B LOGNAME
too;
.IP \(bu 3
sets the terminal's control characters
.RB ( stty ),
shows
.BR /etc/motd ,
says when there is mail, and lists new news items (not for root);
.IP \(bu 3
sets the file creation mask to 022.
.PP
The addition reads every readable file whose name ends in
.B .sh
in
.BR /etc/profile.d ,
so that a package can set up its part of the environment without editing
this file (see
.BR profile.d (4)).
.PP
An update of the base package keeps an edited
.B /etc/profile
and puts the new default beside it as
.BR /etc/profile.new .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/profile
this file.
.TP
.B /etc/profile.d/*.sh
the packages' additions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR profile.d (4),
.BR sh (1),
.BR ksh (1)
